  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated protection support to vulnerable households impacted by the conflict in Ukraine 2024-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Affairs Canada-funded (ICD2722) two-year multi-sectoral project aimed at meeting critical needs of female single-headed and older-single-headed households (SHHs) with children and older dependants in Mkyolaiv, Odesa, and Kharkiv oblasts. Five multi-sectoral teams deliver services: four protection centres (in Kharkiv, Mykolaiv and Odesa) and one mobile team (serving hard-to-reach areas of Kharkiv Oblast). A team of social workers manage protection assessments and coordinate referrals for each household. Support for households will include: child protection and GBV sensitisation; MHPSS services; legal advice; medical support and cash-for-health; MPCA; shelter NFI; light-medium shelter repairs.</narrative>
  </description>
